==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|select|or|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛktə(ɹ)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone or something which [[select]]s or [[choose]]s different [[option]]s.
## {{label|en|cricket}} An [[administrator]] responsible for selecting which [[player]]s will [[play]] for a [[side]].
## {{label|en|internet}} A [[match]]ing [[expression]] in a [[stylesheet]] determining which [[element]]s in the [[markup]] are affected by a [[style]].
## {{label|en|internet}} A [[text]] [[string]] transmitted to a [[Gopher]] [[server]], identifying the [[resource]] to be retrieved.
## {{label|en|computing}} A [[pointer]] to a [[structure]] describing a [[segment]] of [[memory]].
##* '''1990''', ''Byte'' (volume 15, issues 11-13, page 256)
##*: Phar Lap executables {{...}} provide a protected-mode '''selector''', 34h, that maps to the first megabyte of physical memory.
##* '''1995''', Lary L. Myers, ‎Keith Weiskamp, ''Amazing 3-D games adventure set'' (page 235)
##*: You will only have to be concerned with DPMI, '''selectors''', and such, if you use Borland C++ in DOS.

